@startuml
title Supplier Service - Migration-Gated Deployment

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Operator
control "Docker Compose" as Compose
database "Supplier Database\nsupplier-db" as Database
control "Migration Job\nsupplier-migrate" as Migration
control "Supplier API\nsupplier-service" as API

Operator -> Compose: Start supplier deployment
activate Compose
Compose -> Database: Start database container
activate Database

alt Database does not become healthy
  Database --> Compose: Health check fails
  Compose --> Operator: Deployment blocked
else Database becomes healthy
  Database --> Compose: Healthy
  Compose -> Migration: Run alembic upgrade head
  activate Migration
  Migration -> Database: Apply pending revisions

  alt Migration fails
    Database --> Migration: Migration error
    Migration --> Compose: Nonzero exit
    deactivate Migration
    Compose --> Operator: API startup blocked
  else Migration succeeds
    Database --> Migration: Schema at packaged head
    Migration --> Compose: Exit 0
    deactivate Migration
    Compose -> API: Start API container
    activate API

    loop Container health checks
      Compose -> API: GET /ready
      API -> Database: Check connectivity and revision heads
      alt Database and schema are ready
        Database --> API: Matching migration heads
        API --> Compose: 200 OK + ready
      else Database, grants, or schema are not ready
        Database --> API: Readiness check fails
        API --> Compose: 503 Service Unavailable + not_ready
      end
    end

    deactivate API
    Compose --> Operator: Deployment state reported
  end
end

deactivate Database
deactivate Compose

note over Operator,API
  A previously completed migration job does not
  migrate a newly built image automatically; run
  the migration job explicitly on each deployment.
end note

@enduml
